{
 "id": "ls20_understanding",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "shape_decode_loop"
 ],
 "area": "retina",
 "description": "ls20 UNDERSTANDING (block 221000): winning is a SIDE EFFECT of understanding. The curiosity drive (uh_probe_pick, Argmin visits -- least-modelled first, NO goal/win term) routes the agent to probe stations; the 217000 sd-loop recognises each station's transform; uh_mint/uh_confirm/uh_revise build a station->transform MODEL by predict-and-residual (uh_predict is the prediction, the residual is the surprise); uh_deliver_route consults the LEARNED model so winning FALLS OUT. The win_bound (wb_*) control optimises goal-reach directly (Argmin distance-to-goal) with no persistent model -- the labelled baseline the reframe is measured against. Guarded on understand_on==1 (default-OFF, byte-identical otherwise), the arm, and the tick phase. Integer-native; no Rust; reuses the existing shape_decode_loop.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "ls20_understanding",
  "description": "Understand the mechanic; winning is downstream. Curiosity routes to the under-modelled; predict-and-residual grows the model; the goal is never an objective function -- only a thing to model and, once understood, to satisfy as a consequence."
 },
